# Nothing is written of what the lists hold. Where an element under an index goes through an operator the holder is asked in front of the loop for a list of numbers; the element was
# followed to its operator over casts alone. It is followed also over a join of two ways where the other way brings a written number: behind the test that `??` and `||` ask
# (f1 = sumWhole) and out of an arm that a turn may skip (f4 = sumEven). The read gives a raw number or undefined: a hole is no NaN here.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=Array<number>
# CHECK: = HasArrayStorage {{*}} arrayStorage=Double [admitsInt32Storage]
# CHECK: : undefined|number @OptionalDouble = GetArrayElement {{*}} arrayStorage=Double level=Proven
# RUN(EVEN): walk f4 mechanisms=all
# EVEN: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=Array<number>
# EVEN: : undefined|number @OptionalDouble = GetArrayElement {{*}} arrayStorage=Double level=Proven
# RUN(ANSWER): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# ANSWER: sumWhole 6.25 7.25
# ANSWER-NEXT: sumHoled 6.25 7.25
# ANSWER-NEXT: sumMixed 1.2590.75771.5 2.2590.75771.5
# ANSWER-NEXT: sumEven 3.25 4.25
# ANSWER-NEXT: exited with 0
